# The two pieces the holding app was missing (m2/economy-gaps): the LIVING
# family's bunk, which was an empty heading on the slate, and a SECOND generator,
# so the wind is no longer the only power in the game. Then the hole all of that
# was for — a holding out on its own, which could never be staffed at all.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/holding-living.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --give=timber:8,reeds:8,rag:8,wick:4,scrap:10,copper:4,deadwood:4,stone:4
#
# (Everything is built here on the real keys out of the creel — nothing is staged
# with --holding, because the whole claim is that a player can now put these up.
# The hour is daylight on purpose: an array makes nothing after dark, which is
# the point of it, so a tour that proved it at midnight would prove the opposite.)
coast calm
wait 0.6
shot 01-empty-ground-and-a-full-creel with land:coast
# The LIVING family used to be a heading with nothing under it.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
wait 0.4
shot 02-the-living-family-has-a-piece-in-it with app:holding
choose build_bunk
tap use
await made 8
tap pause
await piece:bunk 6
wait 0.6
shot 03-a-bunk-stands-and-its-berths-can-be-seen with piece:bunk, holding
# Room for the next piece, so it is not put up inside the last one.
walk 1,0 1.2
wait 0.4
# The other generator. A spinner is free and unreliable; an array is dear and
# dependable, right up until the sun goes down.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_solar_array
tap use
await made 8
tap pause
await piece:solar_array 6
wait 0.6
shot 04-panels-raked-at-the-sun with piece:solar_array, holding
# And something for it to run, to prove the power is real and not a number in a
# table: a mast has no hands on it and no wind behind it, only daylight.
walk 1,0 1.2
wait 0.4
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_radio_mast
tap use
await made 8
tap pause
await powered 10
wait 0.6
shot 05-a-mast-running-on-daylight-alone with piece:solar_array, piece:radio_mast, powered
#
# --- the hole the LIVING family was for -------------------------------------
#
# `place cliff` is 43 tiles from the nearest village on this seed, past the 34
# within which 35_folk builds any villager body at all — so there is nobody
# walking about out here to ask, which is exactly why a holding here could never
# be staffed however much the player built. `holding_remote` re-asks the world at
# the shutter, so if worldgen ever moves this cliff next to a village the frame
# fails instead of quietly proving nothing.
place cliff
wait 0.8
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_bunk
tap use
await made 8
tap pause
await piece:bunk 6
await holding_remote 4
wait 0.6
shot 06-a-holding-out-on-its-own with piece:bunk, holding_remote, holding
# A plot: work that wants hands, where there are no hands for miles.
walk 1,0 1.2
wait 0.4
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_plot
tap use
await made 8
# The bunk is this holding's first piece and the plot its second, so this is the
# plot's own row. Putting somebody on it is what used to be refused out here.
choose piece_2
tap use
tap pause
await holding_people 10
wait 0.8
shot 07-and-somebody-came-out-to-live-in-it with holding_people, holding_remote, piece:bunk
